  "id": "502004233",
  "subject": [],
  "title": "House of Sallust",
  "provenance": "Pleiades",
  "placeTypeURIs": [
    "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/place-types/townhouse"
  ],
  "details": "<p>The name ascribed to the <em>domus\u00a0</em>derives from an electoral graffito that recommends Caius Sallustius for office. Another, alternative name - this one based on another inscription from the ruins - is the House of A. Cossus Libanus.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "The House of Sallust (VI 2,4) is a domus in Pompeii that assumes its final form around the second century B.C.",
